  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">Gemensamt FN Program Ending Violence phase II</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">UN Joint Programme Ending Violence phase II</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">Detta &#xe4;r ett fortsatt samarbete med UN f&#xf6;r ett gemensamt program/JP f&#xf6;r att stoppa v&#xe5;ld mot kvinnor. UN Women &#xe4;r det ledande organet och UNDP och UNFPA deltar. JP EVaW fokuserar p&#xe5; tre av de fyra pelarna i Istanbulkonventionen: 1) F&#xf6;rhindra alla former av v&#xe5;ld mot kvinnor; 2) S&#xe4;kerst&#xe4;lla effektivt skydd och tillhandah&#xe5;llande av l&#xe4;mpliga tj&#xe4;nster f&#xf6;r &#xf6;verlevande; 3) St&#xf6;dja utvecklingen och genomf&#xf6;randet av en effektiv och integrerad politik f&#xf6;r v&#xe5;ld mot kvinnor. Programmet riktar sig till alla kvinnor och flickor som har utsatts f&#xf6;r v&#xe5;ld. S&#xe4;rskilt fokus l&#xe4;ggs p&#xe5; kvinnor och flickor som uts&#xe4;tts f&#xf6;r diskriminering p&#xe5; flera grunder och intersektionella former. Dessutom engagerar projektet m&#xe4;n och pojkar som centrala f&#xf6;r&#xe4;ndringsagenter f&#xf6;r att fr&#xe4;mja j&#xe4;mst&#xe4;lldhet mellan k&#xf6;nen. UN-organen har ett n&#xe4;ra samarbete med nationella partner, bland annat ministeriet f&#xf6;r h&#xe4;lsa och socialt skydd, justitieministeriet, ungdomsministeriet, utbildningsministeriet, inrikesministeriet, den statliga polisen, lokala myndigheter, nationella m&#xe4;nniskor&#xe4;ttsinstitutioner, medier, det civila samh&#xe4;llet och gr&#xe4;srotsorganisationer.</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This is a continued cooperation with UN for a Joint Programme/JP on ending violence against women. UN Women is the lead agency and UNDP and UNFPA are participating ones. The JP EVaW focuses on three of the four pillars of the Istanbul Convention: 1) Prevent of all forms of VAW; 2) Ensure effective protection and provision of adequate services for survivors; 3) Support the development and implementation of effective and integrated policies on VAW. The programme targets all women and girls who have experienced violence. It places a particular focus on women and girls who are subjected to multiple and intersecting forms of discrimination. Furthermore, the project engages men and boys as pivotal agents of change in the advancement of gender equality. The UN Agencies collaborate closely with national partners, including the Ministry of Health and Social Protection, the Ministry of Justice, the Ministry of Youth, the Ministry of Education, the Ministry of the Interior, the State Police, Local Government Units, National Human Rights Institutions, the media, civil society and grassroots organisations, amongst others.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Project outcomes:
1.Women and girls enjoy more effective preventive measures against violence in Albania. 
2.All women survivors and those at risk are better protected from all forms of violence and have equitable access to services in Albania. 
3.Responsible institutions and actors implement national policies and legislation on VAW in a more comprehensive, inclusive and coordinated way in Albania.</narrative>
  </description>
